    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12257" root="دخل" body-key="d">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَخِلٌ</span></b>  <i>Intrinsically bad</i> or <i>corrupt</i> or <i>unsound:</i>
and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَخْلٌ</span></b>  occurs in the same sense at the end of
a verse: this may be a contraction of the former,
or it may be for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذُو دَخْلٍ</span>. (TA.)

